{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/658990-the-dragon-blooded-retinue","id":658990,"title":"The Dragon Blooded Retinue","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-09T23:06:30-07:00","id":658990,"title":"The Dragon Blooded Retinue","content":"I've been working on a Wood Aspect fresh from the House of Bells who's eager to make a name for himself the past couple of days. One of the coolest things that I think DB players get to do is spend all those Background dots on stuff - thinking up ways to make your Manse background more than just a magic rock or what exactly are the small fluff bits that make your Jade Short Powerbow more than just another identical Jade Short Powerbow.<br /> <br /> In this case, anything killed by Stalker's Bequest is gonna taste DELICIOUS - which is cool when it's deer or something, but takes a turn for the creepy when you kill some bandits.<br /> <br /> But by far the best Backgrounds to gnaw on are ones like Henchmen and Retainers! Yay NPCs that do stuff for you!<br /> <br /> Anyone got any examples of current or former members of your character's retinues they have always wanted to talk about but no one ever gave them the chance to talk about before this elegant and finely crafted thread opened up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T00:47:41-07:00","id":659066,"title":"","content":"So, I played a character called Tepet Al'Vir in a long running DB game, savant/general dude who loved airships, built a fleet, now skytyrant of the Realm.<br /> <br /> In his early adventures he and his circle defended Gem from the Autonthonians by defending a pass that had an old temple to the unconquered sun in it, a fully anatomically correct temple of the unconquered sun....<br /> <br /> Anyway scene setting aside there was fighting going on at all corners, queue the most valuable of the retainers, the cook, who dutifully prepared tea and scones and other sweet things for the party. Granted he occasionally ran away in terror and had to be found and dragged back, because you simply cant fight without refreshment.<br /> <br /> That cook was with the character right up until the end, all the way from Gem to Harbourhead, Thorns. Sijian, Nexus, Halta, Wavecrest, fighting the lover and the hislanti in the north, he grew more of a spine eventually.<br /> <br /> Loved that cook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2325-builder","name":"Builder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T01:19:19-07:00","id":659096,"title":"","content":"A more general question: What sort of retinue would you expect of a traveling Dragon-Blood?<br /> <br /> For example, what sort of servants would I see for a young sworn brotherhood making their way around the Threshold, a single Dragon-Blooded captain in the army returning home, and an established, well-to-do Dragon-Blooded touring their House's estates?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T01:28:24-07:00","id":659101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/658990-the-dragon-blooded-retinue?p=659096#post659096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A more general question: What sort of retinue would you expect of a traveling Dragon-Blood?<br /> <br /> For example, what sort of servants would I see for a young sworn brotherhood making their way around the Threshold, a single Dragon-Blooded captain in the army returning home, and an established, well-to-do Dragon-Blooded touring their House's estates?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is a difficult question because it depends on the house, the individual wealth of the DB and such.<br /> <br /> As an example again Mr Al'Vir in the early days had a cook and a couple of body guards. At the end never travelled anywhere really without a talon of troops, DB bodyguards and a small force of admin and servants, and the cook....<br /> <br /> But in general:<br /> <br /> Single Dragon-Blooded captain in the army - As little as a squire to help with armour and household tasks and maybe as much as the squire, a clerk for the book keeping, a cook and pleasure servant.<br /> <br /> Young sworn brotherhood making their way around the Threshold - Kinda depends on the method of travel but a couple of toughs, a cook, the caravan master, that type of thing.<br /> <br /> Well-to-do Dragon-Blooded touring their House's estates - Think about the entourage that accompanies high level dignataries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2325-builder","name":"Builder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T09:35:10-07:00","id":659449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/658990-the-dragon-blooded-retinue?p=659096#post659096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A more general question: What sort of retinue would you expect of a traveling Dragon-Blood?</div> </div> </div> </div>A relative unExalted Dynast serving as a squire to soak up what being Exalted entails as a 'special tutoring session' to motivate a reluctant student with a young head in the clouds who turns out to be full of hero worship. This could alternatively be modeled as the 'ward' flaw. (mechanically, they could provide social bonuses to Dynastic interactions)<br /> <br /> A middle-aged but stout patrician historian assigned to record your Exalted deeds, but also a source of local and global history for those who haven't read all the tomes they have or didn't pay so much attention in classes. (mechanically they could help with Lore rolls)<br /> <br /> A citizen quartermaster who adequately handles your accounts, mounts, armor and, yes, meals. The quartermaster is constantly worried about money for the consequences of overdrawing promised him by one of your relatives when he was assigned to you, but with no actual power to veto any of your financial decisions. Eventually comes around to seeing money as a tool, not a limit, and will aid your character in acquiring their own funds independent from their House and aid in financial investigations. (mechanically they could substitute for or enhance the resources or contacts backgrounds or aid in specific investigation rolls)<br /> <br /> A peasant from your family's horse farm's first adventure away from home to learn how the stallions' and mares' training holds up to the demands of an Exalted and their retinue. Generally uneducated and hopeless in combat, the peasant has ridden horses since walking and has an uncanny understanding of the animals. Beyond the usual horsemanship you've learned, this retainer can teach you how to truly understand your mount. (mechanically, they could reduce training times for Ride or Ride specialties and reduce the control rating of your party's mounts)<br /> <br /> A slave with a talent for eavesdropping that can be easily disguised as a beggar to learn the local rumors or gauge the charity of other NPCs. (mechanically, they could substitute for a single dot of contacts)<br /> <br /> Of course, you could have either gendered take on the above, and even pair them up since you get several henchmen or retainers. Two historians who love to argue about the finer points of the Seven Tigers Rebellion and the ethics of the deployment of the Imperial Manse, but are the best of friends because nobody else understands why you would even have a stance on such an ancient topic (that they insist is relevant to the current day!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":1103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","user":"Tikor","date":". 09-10-2015, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T12:27:42-07:00","id":659711,"title":"","content":"What about a guy to hold up a mirror to light how awesome you are, and another to beat box as you make your introduction speech?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T13:27:19-07:00","id":659783,"title":"","content":"I would say that a travelling Brotherhood could do with some servants to scout ahead of them, securing accomodations in the next town over, announcing their approach, making arrangements for their reception. Travelling in style tends to entail having everything lavish waiting to be handed to you the moment you arrive, while all of the messy organisational stuff has been discretely handled in the background. It's like going to the opera; some of the magic is lost if you see all of the frantic rearrangement of sets and people being set on their marks directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T07:08:17-07:00","id":661855,"title":"","content":"&quot;Do you really need this many concubines?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T07:16:47-07:00","id":661860,"title":"","content":"Good point, you need concubines, grape-peelers, guys with big palm fronds, and some exotic barbarian slaves (Djala are always popular) to show how rich you are. If you don't look like a Prince of the Earth, how can you expect people to treat you like a Prince of the Earth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T14:28:55-07:00","id":668803,"title":"","content":"If you don't have two maidens with 5-dots in appearance to throw flower petals at you while you sword fight with anathema, you are a bad dynast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T14:36:32-07:00","id":668811,"title":"","content":"You also need <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/comics/2158292/page-41-sitting-with-dragons-attitude/\" target=\"_blank\">purple guys with umbrellas</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T14:42:39-07:00","id":668841,"title":"","content":"A metal golem chef. &quot;Iron Chef, fetch me some fried duck.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T15:10:18-07:00","id":668864,"title":"","content":"Here's how I'd break it down, going by the Followers background:<br /> - *: One body servant, two bodyguards, one roadie (aka, the &quot;do everything&quot; guy), and one administrator.<br /> - **: All of the above, plus four additional roadies, three additional bodyguards, two cooks, two scouts, a doctor, a scholar, and four horse grooms/teamsters.<br /> - ***: One body servant, 10 bodyguards, 20 roadies, 8 cooks, 10 scouts, 2 doctors, 2 scholars, 2 administrators, 20 horse grooms/teamsters, and whatever is appropriate to your business in the remaining slots (hunters, soldiers, harem slaves, etc).<br /> - ****: As ***, but multiplied by 10. Consider rotation of duties.<br /> - *****: Wandering horde.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T19:52:57-07:00","id":670428,"title":"","content":"One of my favorite ideas that I never got to use was about a traveling Dynast, who was a dandy and a fop, but a pretty decent guy, as Dynasts go. He kept his Retainers well-fed, dressed and paid, and was respectful towards them, if a bit comically high-handed.<br /> <br /> Thing is, danger tends to find the Exalted, whether as bandits, behemoths, cults or assassins, and when it did, he would leap into action...which he sucked at. He would inevitably be quickly knocked out by the attackers, if he didn't trip and knock himself out first. If neither, then he'd be &quot;accidentally&quot; knocked out by his own Followers...<br /> <br /> For they kept a secret from their &quot;lord&quot;. In truth, his servants are a Circle of Solar Exalted, who successfully hid their true natures from him, and use him as a key to get all sorts of places they'd have to work to get into normally...as well as to travel in comfort and style! Over time, they've grown quite fond of their &quot;master&quot;, actually respect him in some ways, and certainly don't want to see him actually get hurt or killed. <br /> <br /> So, he comes to after all the action is over, groggily awed to hear his servants describe how he lost himself in his battle-madness and utterly destroyed or drove off the enemy, at which he puffs himself up again, and assures them that he will never allow harm to come to his frail but faithful followers!<br /> <br /> I don't know how long this set-up could actually last in-play, but it always gives me a chuckle...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T17:56:29-07:00","id":671546,"title":"","content":"Hand: I'm reminded of the SMBC Theater skit in which the citizens of Gotham reveal to Batman that they all know that he's Bruce Wayne, and have been putting up with his antics because they felt bad when his parents died.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T18:54:47-07:00","id":671596,"title":"","content":"@Hand-Of-Omega- Sounds like a fun premise for a somewhat silly campaign/one-shot at least!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T22:09:59-07:00","id":671674,"title":"","content":"And the Yeddim is actually somebody's Lunar Mate doing a terrible job of pretending to <i>just</i> be the World's Cleverest Pack Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T07:27:39-07:00","id":671884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/658990-the-dragon-blooded-retinue?p=671546#post671546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hand: I'm reminded of the SMBC Theater skit in which the citizens of Gotham reveal to Batman that they all know that he's Bruce Wayne, and have been putting up with his antics because they felt bad when his parents died.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Heh, I'm not familiar with that one, where can I see it?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T07:53:22-07:00","id":671934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/658990-the-dragon-blooded-retinue?p=671884#post671884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh, I'm not familiar with that one, where can I see it?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=f1-v9VFqztY\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> you go.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T08:07:31-07:00","id":671950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/658990-the-dragon-blooded-retinue?p=671934#post671934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=f1-v9VFqztY\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> you go.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks! Hehe, that's pretty good! &quot;Asshole Style&quot;, someone's gotta write that up for Exalted now!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T13:29:59-07:00","id":672335,"title":"","content":"Well, possibilities are endless, it all depends on one's character and style.<br /> <br /> For example, the last dynast i played, while a graduate of the Spiral Academy was very martial-inclined and something of a show-off to boot, so he was mostly dismissive of the idea of needing bodyguards, as mortal warriors would be pretty much mincemeat against anything that might seriously threaten him, his posturing influencing somewhat his sorceress fiancee, who started to rely in demonic bodyguards in mist form instead of mortal ones, while the rest of the sworn brotherhood felt it was a bit much. <br /> <br /> For actual servants and flunkies he went with (most of them acquired with the game, that started with a kidnapping attempt during graduation, already going on):<br /> <br /> - a southern barbarian versed in a number of tribal dialects from South and West for translator and guide among those idioms or people that wasn't himself familiar with, occasionally doubling as company in the couple sex games.<br /> <br /> - a free Djala that as acrobatic entertainer and singer - and burglar &amp; infiltrator for the occasions the boss wanted him to act unseen.<br /> <br /> - the grandson of a retainer of the PC's father, who served him as secretary to keep order and make copies of his personal business paperwork, diplomatic arrangements and social agenda.<br /> <br /> - a ex-functionary of the Heptagram and friend of his fiance, who needed some help with a new job due to a little case of student pregnancy, became the copyist and scribe of the dynast's occult jounals, studies and correspondence as, though not a sorcerer himself, he had a lot of informal education in the subject from his own household and an interest in artifact-crafting, something he shared with his fiancee in more than one &quot;experimental crafting partnership&quot;. In fact these texts and the correspondence with a number of contacts &amp; allies would gain such a life in the game he eventually set up a small operation to run an occult magazine/newsletter among the Realm's esoteric intelligentsia. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> - a teamster to move around the wagon with his personal master\u2019s workshop (yes, he travels with a workshop to places, just in case he's in the mood).<br /> <br /> - half a dozen artisans with some thaumaturgic knowledge to take care of its contents. Sometime later he had some interesting chances to observe and colaborate with warstrider repair along with a cousin graduated from the House of Bells in a Cathak instalation and used the experience &amp; contacts to get these artisans some extra training so they could serve as aides in artifact construction and warstrider repair.<br /> <br /> Oh yes, there were soldiers for certain, lots of them actually as the brotherhood was involved with going with a legion of reinforcements to a campaign going badly in the southeast but most of my time he was too busy socially smooching to get troop transfers, resources, beenies - or finding whom someone else had to smooch or mollify to get these things - to worry overly much with the actual running of what troops they did get. Too much dealing, gossiping, dueling and intrigue to worry about that boring &quot;not in the middle of a fight yet&quot; stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T18:34:39-07:00","id":672665,"title":"","content":"One PC in a game I played had a retinue of wounded veterans from his army. He's give them crude magical prosthetics if they were injured as a kind of insurance player. He had a legless shaman, a soldier with a magitech finger (he'd ordered the soldier to stick his finger in a lock to see if it was trapped: it was) and a sharkman with no teeth (called Gummy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T19:05:15-07:00","id":672718,"title":"","content":"As an aside a specially silly concept i once did for a dynast was an young Tepet scion that basically seduced himself a literal troop of war widows in a well-intentioned but incredibly ludricous solution of mass reports of the presence of Mara in Tepet lands and the potential threat of the demon developing a major cult and foothold in the region through exploitation of the grief of many. So basically he saved his house from a major infernal infestation by outsluting a soul of Erembour.<br /> <br /> Much to their embarassment.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T19:25:20-07:00","id":672752,"title":"","content":"Perhaps there's a better word to be used than &quot;outslutting.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T19:43:48-07:00","id":672783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/658990-the-dragon-blooded-retinue?p=672752#post672752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps there's a better word to be used than &quot;outslutting.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>True, though none came to me at the time. But let's say &quot;outbedding&quot; them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, he basically made himself a harem-guard of sorts in the process of neutralizing Mara's potential threat to these people, but considering the Sesus have a guard (if not literal legion) of concubine-soldiers, that probably ain't even so shocking depending on what parts of the Isle one is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-20-2015, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T01:28:52-07:00","id":672993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/658990-the-dragon-blooded-retinue?p=672665#post672665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One PC in a game I played had a retinue of wounded veterans from his army. He's give them crude magical prosthetics if they were injured as a kind of insurance player. He had a legless shaman, a soldier with a magitech finger (he'd ordered the soldier to stick his finger in a lock to see if it was trapped: it was) and a sharkman with no teeth (called Gummy).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Amusingly they weren't soldiers from his army and he didn't pay for he magical prosthetics either","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2325-builder","name":"Builder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T02:32:50-07:00","id":673018,"title":"","content":"Good point, I forgot that at that point he was still just your subordinate, so they were yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T05:47:35-07:00","id":673088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/658990-the-dragon-blooded-retinue?p=673018#post673018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point, I forgot that at that point he was still just your subordinate, so they were yours.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then he stole them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2325-builder","name":"Builder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T05:55:14-07:00","id":673093,"title":"","content":"Again speaking of retainers, followers and other hanger-ons choices, beside defining what each minion or group is good for, working out early on with the ST where they come from or why they got good at their function can be nice and useful for both roleplaying fodder and the occasional off-the-cuff contact or hook one might provide through them.<br /> <br /> In the case of the retinue i described previously, the secretary had strong ties to the PC's household through his own family fortunes and so was as familiar with some of its members, tastes and internal gossip as him, beside occasionally serving as discrete messenger (if not observer) of the house elders in his projects and businesses, meanwhile his scribe for esoterica, beside being a personal friend of his fiancee, provided with some info on Island of Voices, a few minor contacts and some juicy (if slightly outdated) Heptagram scandals.<br /> <br /> The artisans are interesting in that they started generic but acquired detailing along the way of a convoluted subplot centered around recovering the heavily damaged warstrider of a NPC's disappeared (possibly dead) mother for repairs, somehow receiving <b>another</b> damaged warstrider due to a &quot;clerical mistake&quot; with the Wyld Hunt and visiting the Cloister of Wisdom with the aforementioned Cathak crew to basically steal the warstrider under the Order's mose through the cover of correcting the papers (except we <b>didn't</b> return the other warstrider in the end) and providing a month-long seminary on warstriders, their maitenance and repair on the temple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T10:01:04-07:00","id":673279,"title":"","content":"I ended up with a small group of retainers, all of whom were former immaculates who had been cast out of the Order for breaking their oaths, one had a child, one gambled, one attacked another monk, one wouldn't follow dietary restrictions correctly, one had his tongue removed for being a heretic but was repentant, etc. All of them still wanted to live correctly according to the Immaculate Philosophy but they've stumbled on the way, so my Exalt took them under his wing and is trying to help them walk the proper path for mortals. All told they act as his bodyguards, a couple teamsters/valets and his secretary and their narrative role is essentially to orbit him and smooth out his life (plucking the hidden razor blades from the candyfloss of life is my favorite euphemism for this)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T10:26:17-07:00","id":673290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/658990-the-dragon-blooded-retinue?p=673279#post673279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ended up with a small group of retainers, all of whom were former immaculates who had been cast out of the Order for breaking their oaths, one had a child, one gambled, one attacked another monk, one wouldn't follow dietary restrictions correctly, one had his tongue removed for being a heretic but was repentant, etc. All of them still wanted to live correctly according to the Immaculate Philosophy but they've stumbled on the way, so my Exalt took them under his wing and is trying to help them walk the proper path for mortals. All told they act as his bodyguards, a couple teamsters/valets and his secretary and their narrative role is essentially to orbit him and smooth out his life (plucking the hidden razor blades from the candyfloss of life is my favorite euphemism for this)</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of former immaculates made remember that, even though he was probably the most actually devout dynast among the PCs, my character had no actual monks among his retainers, though that probably in part because as a dragon-blood it would be strange to have a non-exalted immaculate for spiritual support and never actually thought of even looking for one due to all the stuff the group busied itself with in their war campaigning buildup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}